{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_qmn_synergy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_qmn_synergy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Shared.MarkovTraceClaim"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_qmn_synergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_qmn_synergy","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L84-L124","doc":"**Proposition statement** (from manuscript):\n\nThe Wenzl-bridge ([y-lambda-closed-form](#prop:y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge))\ngives $y_\\lambda(q)$ as a closed q-rational expression in $\\sqrt q$\nin $O(p(n) \\cdot \\max\\text{hooks})$ time, while q-Murnaghan-Nakayama\n([Halverson-Ram 1995, Wenzl q-MN as in `q_mn_canonical.py`]) gives\n$\\chi_\\lambda(T_w; q)$ for canonical permutation braids $T_w$ in\n$O(n^2)$ time.*\n\n*Combining them gives the Markov trace*\n\n$$\n  \\mathrm{tr}_M(T_w) \\;=\\; \\sum_{\\lambda \\,\\vdash\\, n} y_\\lambda(q) \\cdot \\chi_\\lambda(T_w; q)\n$$\n\n*on canonical permutation braids in $O(p(n) \\cdot (\\max\\text{hooks} + n^2))$\ntime — far faster than the Hoefsmit-seminormal path\n($O(p(n) \\cdot \\dim_\\lambda^2 \\cdot \\ell(w))$).*\n\n## Why this is significant\n\nThree orthogonal speedups combine:\n\n| Quantity | Old path | New path | Speedup |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $y_\\lambda(q)$ | Linear-system solve, sympy 20-min timeout @ n=5 | Wenzl-bridge, ~0.3 s @ n=12 | $\\sim 10^4 \\times$ |\n| $\\chi_\\lambda(T_w; q)$ canonical | Hoefsmit $O(\\dim_\\lambda^2 \\cdot \\ell(w))$ | q-MN $O(n^2)$ | $10^2 \\times$ at $n = 12$ |\n| $\\mathrm{tr}_M$ on closed braid | Direct seminormal matrix-trace | $\\sum y_\\lambda \\chi_\\lambda$ via above | combined $10^6 \\times$ |\n\nFor atom-knot identification at $n = 18$ ($p(n) = 385$, $\\max\\dim_\\lambda \\approx 1000$) or $n = 21$ ($p(n) = 792$, $\\max\\dim_\\lambda \\approx 5000$),\nthis drops the per-isotope compute time from\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the manuscript claim over a context class and discharges it from the class's fields (§3b-conditional). The declaration type-checks as a complete term; the substantive mathematical content is carried by the context-class axioms, and a full derivation from substrate primitives remains pending. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:wenzl-qmn-synergy","label":"prop:wenzl-qmn-synergy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.claim_combined_speedup_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.claim_combined_speedup_bound","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Manuscript boxed identity — Combined speedup is the product of\northogonal speedups, bounded below by `10⁶×`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.claim_ii_mass_formula_compute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.claim_ii_mass_formula_compute","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (ii) — q-MN speedup `≥ 10²×`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.claim_i_direct_verification_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.claim_i_direct_verification_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (i) — Wenzl-bridge speedup `≥ 10⁴×`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.combined_speedup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.combined_speedup","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Combined speedup factor (`= wenzl_speedup · qmn_speedup`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.qmn_speedup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.qmn_speedup","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Speedup factor of q-MN vs Hoefsmit characters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.wenzl_speedup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.wenzl_speedup","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Speedup factor of Wenzl bridge vs linear-system solve.\n\nKept at `ℝ` deliberately (§7c): the speedup fields are *measured*\nwall-clock ratios and their sub-claims are order comparisons\n(`10000 ≤ …`), which is archimedean content sitting after the\nsubstrate→archimedean wall.  Only the trace fields below move to the\ninherited generic ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.toMarkovTraceContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext.toMarkovTraceContext","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L22-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlQmnSynergyContext","kind":"class","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/wenzl_qmn_synergy.lean#L19-L72","doc":"Abstract context for the `wenzl_qmn_synergy` claim — manuscript-named\ntyped fields below; the `holds` field carries the `Prop`-valued\nclaim of the lemma. ","signatureChunk":0}]}